        "rating": 1,
        "relative_time_description": "6 months ago",
        "text": "This past Saturday I had the worst experience with an incompetent employee at Club De Golf Vaudreuil, which later I found out that this same employee was the owner/bosses son. So my girlfriend and I walk into the clubhouse and paid for our rounds, the employee at the front desk then told my girlfriend that she needed to change as her golf attire was too revealing. I found this very strange as I have been playing golf at this course for years now and all of a sudden they’ve implemented a strict dress code for a “public” golf course… mind you my girlfriend is wearing a golf/tennis outfit. We then said oh well and decided to purchase a polo they had on display in the clubhouse. We grabbed some food and grabbed our golf cart and made our way to the first hole. Drivers in hand and ready to tee off we notice the owners son lurking about in his cart. I had asked him about the new dress code before leaving for the start of our round and everything seemed fine. He even saw us off with 1 golf bag and the both of us leaving for the first hole. As I was about to tee off he then came over and said we couldn’t play this course with only 1 set of clubs. Confused I questioned him as he saw us off and mind you I’ve been playing this course for years and have had friends of mine who were beginners use my clubs with no issues. At this point we are under the assumption that he is trying to gouge us for money as there were no rules posted anywhere on the course about using one golf bag. I asked him where the rules were and he couldn’t give me a straight answer, nor could he even formulate a proper response in English. We recommend that no one play this course as you will be hounded for money, treated unprofessionally. To have a strict dress code for a public course, especially Vaudreuil is laughable, especially when they can barely keep their course in good condition. Vaudreuil is a course where you play if you’re new to the game, can’t get a tee time at anywhere else and don’t mind the course being in horrible shape. It’s a cheap price for the weekends. They turn away new golfers who want to try a new activity. Judging by the other reviews on here like father like son.",
